name: Actual license signals retain repetitions, deferred review, partial history and readable recovery
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/license_audit.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: setg ui.auto_open_viz false
submit: logs
submit: run license-scan:scan {"requireSpdxHeaders":false}
require-live-snap: 35 license-scan: 1 finding | first-scan
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/license_audit.py @TMP_TARGET @ART first
submit: run license-scan:scan {"requireSourceSpdxHeaders":false}
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/license_audit.py @TMP_TARGET @ART second
require-live-snap: 35 run receipt | second-scan
submit: run license-scan:scan {"require_source_spdx_headers":false}
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/license_audit.py @TMP_TARGET @ART third
require-live-snap: 35 run receipt | third-scan
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 Package manifest does not declare a license | actual-finding
expect: signal-only
ask: Do three explicit scanner repetitions produce one retained finding with real source evidence and distinct observations, while keeping generated analysis artifacts outside source policy?
submit: decision deferred Owned license policy needs owner review
require-live-snap: 25 recorded: deferred | deferred-finding
expect: recorded: deferred
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/license_audit.py @TMP_TARGET @ART deferred
resize: 160x48
live-snap: review-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: review-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: review-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: review-60x20
nav-mode:
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 F-0001 · FINDING | finding-reader
resize: 40x12
live-snap: review-40x12
expect: F-0001
expect: PgUp/PgDn read
keys: NPage
live-snap: finding-page-1-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: finding-page-2-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: finding-page-3-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: finding-page-4-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: finding-page-5-40x12
keys: NPage
live-snap: finding-page-6-40x12
expect: F-0001
expect: PgUp/PgDn read
ask: Are the real policy observation, signal-only evidence and scripted deferral readable through normal Review controls across six terminal sizes without claiming a verified vulnerability?
resize: 120x36
keys: q
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/license_audit.py @TMP_TARGET @ART license
submit: logs
submit: run sast:scan {"taskMode":"manual","tasks":["license-scan"],"triage":false,"verify":false,"autoPatch":false}
require-live-snap: 25 PREREQUISITE PLAN | deterministic-prerequisite
expect: no model cost expected
keys: a
require-live-snap: 35 0 finding(s) | clean-rerun
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/license_audit.py @TMP_TARGET @ART clean
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 not observed | retained-observation
expect: recorded: deferred
expect: Absence does not establish a fix.
ask: Does a clean rerun after an explicit source edit retain earlier observations and deferral without silently marking the finding fixed or making an old decision current?
submit: report
require-live-snap: 25 Enter export | report
keys: j j j
require-live-snap: 20 format json | json-report
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 EXPORTED | report-exported
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/license_audit.py @TMP_TARGET @ART exported
ask: Does the exported report retain the source-bound deferral and absence limitation from actual scanner observations?
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/license_audit.py @TMP_TARGET @ART oversize
submit: logs
submit: run license-scan:scan {"requireSourceSpdxHeaders":false}
require-live-snap: 35 2097152 | failed-license-read
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/license_audit.py @TMP_TARGET @ART failed
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 Owned license policy needs owner review | retained-after-failure
expect: recorded: deferred
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/license_audit.py @TMP_TARGET @ART repair
submit: logs
submit: run sast:scan {"taskMode":"manual","tasks":["license-scan"],"triage":false,"verify":false,"autoPatch":false}
require-live-snap: 25 PREREQUISITE PLAN | cached-prerequisite
expect: cached via context:build
keys: r
require-live-snap: 35 0 finding(s) | recovered-scan
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/license_audit.py @TMP_TARGET @ART recovered
ask: Does an oversized license file produce an honest failed result, retain earlier evidence and recover only after explicit repair and rerun?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1 KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 KUZUSHI | restarted
submit: open F-0001
require-live-snap: 25 Owned license policy needs owner review | recovered-review
expect: not observed
expect: recorded: deferred
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/license_audit.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart retain all six real scanner outcomes, three observations, one scripted review decision and the report without executing source, calling a model or inventing fix evidence?
keys: C-c
require-exit: 10
